# Turf Monster

> Turf Monster is a skill-based sports pick'em game. A player picks a set of teams; each team earns the points it scores multiplied by its Turf Score. An AI agent can play for one player through a JSON API, using an API key the player creates.

If you are an agent about to play for someone, read the agent guide in full before making any request that spends something.

## For agents

- [Agent guide (Markdown)](<%= agent_base_url %><%= agents_guide_markdown_path %>): the rules, scoring, locks, prizes, eligibility, every endpoint and error, retries, and how to reason about a lineup.
- API base URL: <%= agent_base_url %>/api/v1 (send `Authorization: Bearer <key>` on every request)
- MCP endpoint: <%= agent_mcp_url %> (the same API as <%= AgentMcp::Tools::ALL.size %> tools, for a client that can send the same `Authorization` header, such as Claude Code; see "Playing through MCP" in the guide)

## For people

- [Play with your AI assistant](<%= agent_base_url %><%= agents_path %>): a starter prompt to copy, three steps to get a key, and the command that connects Claude Code.
- [Agent guide (page)](<%= agent_base_url %><%= agents_guide_path %>): the same guide, formatted.
